;; Written 2026-10-19 by Claude, from the guest runs (Phase 18 step 6d),
;; for the user's review. Why this is right:
;; - The program built from poc's objects (tools/vax-suite's O<n>
;;   builds). Its fault and its place are those of expected-vax-
;;   notrap-10.err, which says why; only the traceback differs, since
;;   poc's objects carry traceback and debugger records (vax-object-
;;   language.md, section 16) and MACRO's carry none: each routine in
;;   poc's code has its line, 74, case 9's statement, which faults.
;; - The module's code is named NOTRAP_INIT, its routine's own name,
;;   where MACRO's objects have only the label POC_CODE before it.
;; - The module's start (_MAIN) is poc's own code, with no source line.
;; - The same under -O2 and -OC, so for every build.
%SYSTEM-F-FLTDIV_F, arithmetic fault, floating divide by zero at PC=xxxxxxxx, PSL=xxxxxxxx
%TRACE-F-TRACEBACK, symbolic stack dump follows
module name     routine name                     line       rel PC    abs PC

NOTRAP          NOTRAP_INIT                        74      xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
NOTRAP          NOTRAP_MAIN                                xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
